.el .ds Aq '
.TH b4-payees-list 1  "b4 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
b4\-payees\-list \- List payees
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBb4 payees list\fR [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-filter\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-header\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
List payees
.PP
List the payees saved in the vault\*(Aqs address book, ordered by name (ignoring case; letters outside A to Z, such as umlauts, come after Z).
.PP
Table output shows name, IBAN, BIC, bank, town and the number of bookings of each payee. The other formats carry every column of the `payees` table under its own name (see `b4 schema payees`), followed by `booking_count`.
.PP
Bookings do not refer to an address book entry; they only carry the name of the other party. `booking_count` is therefore a match by name: the number of bookings whose payee name equals the payee\*(Aqs name, ignoring case and surrounding blanks. Payees that share a name share the number, and a booking that spells the name differently is not counted. Every booking counts once: a split booking or a collective booking counts as its parts, not as parts plus the whole. Pending bookings are included.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-filter\fR \fI<TEXT>\fR
Only payees with TEXT in one of their text fields, ignoring case

Keeps the payees that have TEXT as a substring of their name, IBAN, BIC, account number, bank code, address, bank name or address, default purpose, default category, e\-mail address, customer number or notes. Upper and lower case are the same. TEXT is taken literally: `%` and `_` are ordinary characters. An IBAN is also found when TEXT has blanks in it.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR [default: ./b4.duckdb]
Database file: written by `decrypt`, read by every other command
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBB4_DB\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR
Output format [default: table]

table is made for reading: line breaks, control characters and text direction overrides in the data are replaced. csv, jsonl and json are data: written to a file or a pipe they are exact, byte for byte. Only when they are written to a terminal are the characters a terminal acts on (escape sequences, text direction overrides) made harmless: csv shows U+FFFD in their place, json and jsonl write them as \\uXXXX escapes.

In json and jsonl a number that a double cannot hold exactly is a string of its digits: an integer beyond 2^53, a decimal of more than 15 significant digits.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
table: Aligned text, fitted to the terminal
.IP \(bu 2
json: One JSON array of objects
.IP \(bu 2
jsonl: One JSON object per line
.IP \(bu 2
csv: Comma\-separated values with a header line
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-header\fR
Leave out the header line of table and csv output
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Do not print informational messages to stderr

Silences progress and summary lines and the "no rows" note. Warnings and errors are still printed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
b4 payees list
    List all saved payees.
b4 payees list \-\-filter versicherung
    Payees with "versicherung" in one of their fields.
b4 payees list \-\-filter \(aqDE49 9999\(aq
    Payees whose IBAN contains DE499999.
b4 payees list \-\-output csv > payees.csv
    Every stored field of every payee, as CSV.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBb4\fR(1),
\fBb4\-payees\fR(1)
